SAT_CHUNK("rw/text-structure/2/0",[
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.1a97d62a8e","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data1-1","passage":"<p class=\"src\">The following text is from a novel.</p><p>Mrs. Achebe had taught piano in the same small room for forty years. The upright piano had a cracked key and a pedal that squeaked, and every student eventually asked why she did not replace it. She always gave the same answer: a perfect instrument forgives too much. On this one, she said, you have to listen.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best states the main purpose of the text?","choices":["To contrast the teaching methods of two piano teachers","To explain why a character decided to stop teaching","To reveal a character's view about the value of an imperfect instrument","To describe the process of repairing an old piano"],"answer":"C","explanation":"The details about the flawed piano set up her explanation of why she keeps it. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.d488e05aac","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data1-2","passage":"<p>Many people assume that desert plants survive by storing large amounts of water. Some do, but a surprising number take a different approach. Certain desert shrubs drop nearly all of their leaves during dry months, reducing the surface through which water can escape. When rain returns, they grow a new set of leaves within days and resume making food. For these plants, survival depends less on saving water than on knowing when to stop using it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the first sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It provides evidence for the claim made in the final sentence.","It defines a term that the text uses throughout.","It describes a finding that researchers later confirmed.","It introduces a common belief that the rest of the text qualifies."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The text says \"some do, but\" and then describes a different strategy. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.a9cd699e16","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data1-5","passage":"<p class=\"src\">The following text is from a short story.</p><p>The storm had taken the power at dusk, and by nine the house was silent except for the wind. Jalen's little sister had stopped crying an hour ago, mostly because he had turned the flashlight into a stage light and was performing every animal voice he knew. He ran out of animals around eleven. By then she was asleep, and he sat in the dark holding the flashlight, listening to the windows rattle and wishing someone would do the same for him.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the final sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It reveals that the character who has been reassuring someone else is also in need of reassurance.","It suggests that Jalen's sister is only pretending to be asleep.","It explains why the power went out during the storm.","It shows that the storm has finally ended."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The last detail reveals Jalen's own fear. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.cd68c47e17","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data1-6","passage":"<p>For most of the twentieth century, many linguists regarded the \"uptalk\" pattern, in which statements end with a rising pitch, as a sign of uncertainty. More recent studies complicate this view. In recorded conversations, speakers who used rising pitch often did so while holding the floor, signaling that they had more to say, or while checking that listeners were following along. Rather than expressing doubt, the rise frequently seemed to invite engagement.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?","choices":["It describes an experiment and then explains why its results were rejected.","It defines a speech pattern and then traces its geographic spread.","It argues that rising pitch should be avoided in formal speech.","It presents a traditional interpretation and then describes findings that challenge it."],"answer":"D","explanation":"Older view, then \"more recent studies complicate this view.\" The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.5513b4b633","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data1-7","passage":"<p>In 1928, the town of Eastbridge replaced its wooden footbridge with a concrete one. The new bridge was stronger, but residents soon noticed that the swallows that had nested beneath the old bridge for generations were gone. The birds' mud nests could not cling to the smooth concrete. In 2019, volunteers attached rough wooden panels to the underside of the bridge. The following spring, the swallows returned.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best states the main purpose of the text?","choices":["To explain how a change in a bridge's material affected nesting birds and how that effect was reversed","To describe how swallows build nests from mud","To argue that towns should build bridges from wood rather than concrete","To trace the complete history of bridge construction in Eastbridge"],"answer":"A","explanation":"Cause (smooth concrete), effect (swallows left), and fix (rough panels). The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.8331059e97","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data1-9","passage":"<p class=\"src\">The following text is adapted from a travel essay.</p><p>The market opens before the sun does. By five, vendors have unfolded their tables and arranged pyramids of oranges and bundles of herbs still wet with dew. By seven, the aisles are so crowded that shoppers move sideways. By noon it is over: the tables fold, the tarps come down, and a street cleaner sweeps away the last crushed petals. An hour later, no one walking by would guess that a thousand people had passed through that morning.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?","choices":["It follows a market through a single morning in chronological order.","It explains how vendors at the market set their prices.","It compares two markets in different cities.","It describes a market and then argues that it should be moved."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The time markers \"by five,\" \"by seven,\" \"by noon,\" and \"an hour later\" show chronological order. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.347897d0bc","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data1-10","passage":"<p>Octopuses have a remarkable ability to taste with their arms. Each arm is lined with suckers containing thousands of chemical receptors, allowing an octopus to detect prey hidden in crevices simply by touching the surrounding rock. Researchers have also found that an arm can begin reacting to a promising scent before the octopus's central brain appears to direct it, suggesting that each arm processes some information on its own.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the final sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It explains why octopuses hide in crevices.","It contradicts the claim made in the first sentence.","It introduces a different animal for comparison.","It presents a finding that extends the text's description of the octopus's arms."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The last sentence adds that arms may process information on their own. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.2fed79dc60","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data1-12","passage":"<p>Glass frogs, found in Central and South American rain forests, have translucent skin on their undersides. For years, scientists assumed this transparency simply helped the frogs blend in with the leaves they rest on. A recent study found something more surprising: while sleeping, a glass frog moves most of its red blood cells into its liver, making its body far more transparent. When the frog wakes and becomes active, the blood cells return to circulation.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the second sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It explains why glass frogs are found only in rain forests.","It presents an earlier understanding that the study's finding goes beyond.","It describes the method the researchers used in their study.","It offers a conclusion that the rest of the text supports."],"answer":"B","explanation":"\"For years, scientists assumed\" sets up \"a recent study found something more surprising.\" The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.43d80e3ce1","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data1-14","passage":"<p>A team of volunteers in a coastal town spent a summer recording every species of bird they saw along a single kilometer of shoreline. They expected to count perhaps thirty species. They counted seventy-two. Several were migrants resting for only a day or two, which the volunteers would have missed if they had visited less often. The team concluded that frequent, repeated observation reveals far more about a place than occasional surveys do.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the sentence \"They counted seventy-two\" in the text as a whole?","choices":["It questions the accuracy of the volunteers' count.","It lists the most common species along the shoreline.","It reveals that the result far exceeded the volunteers' expectations.","It explains the method the volunteers used to count birds."],"answer":"C","explanation":"It follows \"They expected to count perhaps thirty species.\" The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.bec1fd92fa","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data1-18","passage":"<p>When engineers designed a new high-speed train, they faced an unexpected problem: each time the train exited a tunnel at full speed, it produced a loud boom that disturbed nearby residents. The cause was air compressed in front of the train's blunt nose. An engineer who was also a birdwatcher noticed that kingfishers dive from air into water, a much denser medium, with barely a splash. The team redesigned the train's nose to resemble a kingfisher's long, narrow beak, and the booms largely stopped.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the third sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It suggests that kingfishers are disturbed by trains.","It describes an observation that inspired a solution to the problem.","It explains why residents complained about the train.","It presents a second problem the engineers faced."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The kingfisher observation led to the redesigned nose. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.f0128cbe27","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data1-19","passage":"<p>Scientists studying tree rings from a forest in a dry region found that rings formed during years of heavy rainfall were noticeably wider than rings from drought years. By measuring rings in trees that were hundreds of years old, the team reconstructed a record of rainfall stretching back far earlier than any written weather records from the area. The reconstruction revealed several long droughts that had not previously been documented.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?","choices":["It compares two forests and explains why one grew faster.","It describes a drought and its effects on local farmers.","It describes a relationship between tree rings and rainfall and then explains what scientists learned by using it.","It questions whether tree rings can reveal information about the past."],"answer":"C","explanation":"The ring-rainfall link, then the reconstruction and its findings. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.ccefd766d4","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data2-32","passage":"<p>Scientists once assumed that honeybees navigate mainly by remembering landmarks. Experiments have shown that bees also rely on the position of the sun, and they can compensate for the sun's movement across the sky over the course of a day. Even when clouds hide the sun, bees can detect patterns of polarized light in patches of blue sky, allowing them to keep their bearings.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the first sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It presents an earlier view that the following sentences show to be incomplete.","It states the main conclusion of the experiments.","It describes a method for studying bees.","It explains why bees need to navigate."],"answer":"A","explanation":"Later sentences show bees use more than landmarks. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.a1e4c4640f","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data2-33","passage":"<p>In the 1800s, many cities drew drinking water directly from rivers that also carried sewage. Outbreaks of cholera were common. When one city began filtering its water through layers of sand and gravel, cholera cases there dropped sharply, while a neighboring city that continued using unfiltered river water saw no such decline. The comparison helped persuade officials elsewhere to adopt filtration.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the third sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It argues that filtration was too expensive for most cities.","It introduces a disease different from cholera.","It presents a contrast that provides evidence for the effectiveness of filtration.","It explains how sand filters are built."],"answer":"C","explanation":"The two-city comparison is the evidence that persuaded officials. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.878f7d321c","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data2-35","passage":"<p>Many cities have begun replacing streetlights with LED bulbs, which use far less electricity than older lamps. Some astronomers and ecologists have raised a concern: early LED streetlights emitted a large amount of blue light, which scatters widely in the atmosphere and can disrupt the behavior of nocturnal animals. Newer LED designs produce warmer light with less blue, offering energy savings with fewer side effects.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?","choices":["It compares the costs of several kinds of lighting.","It explains how streetlights are manufactured.","It describes a change, raises a concern about it, and then explains how the concern has been addressed.","It argues that cities should return to older lamps."],"answer":"C","explanation":"LED adoption, blue-light concern, warmer newer designs. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.4fb31ad86d","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data2-36","passage":"<p>When a regional airline began weighing passengers' carry-on bags at the gate, travelers complained about the delays. The airline explained that its small planes have strict weight limits, and knowing the total weight of luggage helps pilots calculate how much fuel to carry. Within a few months, passengers adjusted by packing lighter, and boarding times returned to normal.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the second sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It suggests that the policy was unnecessary.","It describes how passengers reacted to the policy.","It gives the reason behind the policy that caused the complaints.","It explains how pilots are trained."],"answer":"C","explanation":"The weight limits and fuel calculations explain why bags were weighed. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.5ad65de8e1","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data2-38","passage":"<p class=\"src\">The following text is from a novel.</p><p>For three generations the Okonkwo family had run the hardware store on Main Street, and for three generations the bell above its door had rung the same flat note. When Adaeze took over the shop, she replaced the dusty shelves, repainted the walls a pale green, and installed bright new lights. But when a customer suggested she replace the bell, she shook her head. Some things, she said, should sound exactly the way they always have.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?","choices":["It presents a customer's complaint and the store's response.","It describes several changes a character makes and then one thing she decides not to change.","It compares two family members' approaches to business.","It describes a store's history and then its closing."],"answer":"B","explanation":"New shelves, paint, and lights contrast with the kept bell. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.134471e278","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data3-41","passage":"<p>Many people picture icebergs as white, but some are strikingly blue. The color comes from ice that formed under great pressure deep within a glacier. That pressure squeezes out the tiny air bubbles that normally scatter all colors of light and make ice look white. Without those bubbles, the dense ice absorbs more red light than blue, so blue light is what reaches our eyes.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?","choices":["It points out a surprising observation and then explains its cause step by step.","It lists several types of glaciers and their locations.","It compares icebergs in two different oceans.","It describes an experiment and then questions its results."],"answer":"A","explanation":"Blue icebergs (observation), then pressure, bubbles, and light absorption (explanation). The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.08c5c65aa3","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data3-42","passage":"<p>Historians studying a seventeenth-century merchant's account books noticed that his profits rose sharply in the years after he began recording every transaction, however small, in a single ledger. Earlier, he had kept separate notebooks for each ship and often lost track of debts owed to him. The historians suggest that the change in record keeping, rather than any change in the goods he traded, may explain his improved fortunes.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the second sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It suggests that the historians' conclusion is incorrect.","It describes the merchant's earlier practice, which helps explain why the change mattered.","It presents evidence that the merchant traded different goods over time.","It explains how historians located the account books."],"answer":"B","explanation":"Separate notebooks and lost debts contrast with the later single ledger. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.603af9129e","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data3-45","passage":"<p>For years, a small theater company performed classic plays in their original formal language. Attendance slowly declined. When a new director proposed staging the same plays with modern costumes and settings while keeping every original word, longtime members worried that the changes would distract from the text. Instead, audiences grew, and several reviewers wrote that the unfamiliar settings made them listen to the familiar words more closely than ever.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?","choices":["It compares acting styles in two theater companies.","It describes a decline, a proposed change and the concern it raised, and then the unexpected result.","It argues that modern plays are better than classic ones.","It traces the history of a single classic play."],"answer":"B","explanation":"Declining attendance, proposal and worry, then growth and positive reviews. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.98a9cfc493","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data3-49","passage":"<p class=\"src\">The following text is adapted from a nineteenth-century travel diary.</p><p>We reached the pass at noon, and the guide told us to rest. I could not. Before me the valley opened like a book whose pages I had waited all my life to read: the river glinting silver, the villages no larger than thumbprints, and beyond them, rank upon rank, mountains I had known only from maps. My legs ached, but I stood until the guide took my arm and insisted that I sit.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the comparison of the valley to \"a book\" in the text?","choices":["It explains how the maps of the region were made.","It conveys the writer's long-held eagerness to see the landscape.","It suggests that the writer is reading while resting.","It emphasizes that the valley is small and ordinary."],"answer":"B","explanation":"Pages \"I had waited all my life to read\" express anticipation. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.fd5ed0d4b1","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data3-52","passage":"<p>When a zoo redesigned its gorilla habitat, keepers replaced the concrete floor with soil, logs, and tall grasses and scattered food throughout the space instead of placing it in a single pile. Within months, the gorillas spent far more time exploring and foraging and far less time sitting idle. The keepers also observed fewer conflicts among the animals, perhaps because food was no longer concentrated in one spot that dominant gorillas could control.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?","choices":["It describes changes to a habitat and then reports the effects of those changes.","It argues that zoos should release gorillas into the wild.","It compares gorillas in the wild with gorillas in zoos.","It explains how gorillas choose their leaders."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The redesign, then more activity and fewer conflicts. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.7399653c93","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data3-53","passage":"<p>Early photographs often show people with stiff, serious expressions. It is tempting to conclude that people in the nineteenth century were more solemn than people today. But early cameras required subjects to stay perfectly still for many seconds, sometimes minutes, and holding a natural smile that long is difficult. Many portrait traditions of the time also associated dignity with a calm, composed face.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the second sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It explains why portrait traditions valued calm faces.","It presents a tempting conclusion that the rest of the text challenges.","It describes how early cameras worked.","It provides evidence that supports the final sentence."],"answer":"B","explanation":"\"It is tempting to conclude\" is followed by \"But,\" which offers other explanations. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.9ba86296fd","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data3-55","passage":"<p class=\"src\">The following text is from a short story.</p><p>Priya had practiced the violin piece for months, but in the recital hall her hands shook so badly that the first notes wavered. She thought of stopping. Then she noticed her grandfather in the third row, eyes closed, head tilted slightly, the way he listened to the radio on Sunday mornings. She drew the bow again, and this time the note held steady.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the third sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It describes a moment that marks a turning point in Priya's performance.","It describes the recital hall in detail.","It explains why Priya began playing the violin.","It reveals that Priya's grandfather disapproves of her playing."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The image of her grandfather comes just before her playing steadies. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.1c1c833875","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data3-63","passage":"<p>For most of history, sailors navigated by the stars, but measuring longitude at sea remained extremely difficult. Longitude depends on knowing the time at a reference location while at sea, and ordinary clocks of the era lost accuracy on rolling ships. The problem was largely solved when clockmakers designed timekeepers precise and sturdy enough to keep accurate time through storms and temperature changes, allowing navigators to calculate their position far more reliably.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?","choices":["It describes the life of a famous sailor.","It compares navigation by stars with navigation by maps.","It argues that clocks were more important than ships.","It identifies a problem, explains why it was difficult, and describes how it was solved."],"answer":"D","explanation":"Longitude problem, reason (clocks on ships), solution (precise timekeepers). The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.2ad3692a27","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data3-66","passage":"<p>Wind turbines are often placed on ridges and hilltops, where winds are strongest. Some wildlife biologists raised concerns that turbines in such locations could harm migrating birds of prey, which ride the same updrafts along ridges. A study tracking hawks and eagles near one wind farm found that collisions were concentrated at a few turbines positioned directly in the birds' main flight corridors. Shutting down those turbines during peak migration weeks reduced collisions sharply while cutting the farm's yearly energy production by less than one percent.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?","choices":["It argues that wind energy is too harmful to continue.","It explains a concern, reports a finding that clarifies the problem, and describes an effective solution.","It describes the migration routes of hawks in detail.","It compares energy production at several wind farms."],"answer":"B","explanation":"Concern, concentrated collisions, targeted shutdowns. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.fcc78e9670","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data4-68","passage":"<p>Sea levels were far lower during the last ice age, when enormous amounts of water were locked in glaciers. Areas that are now shallow seas were once dry land. Archaeologists have begun searching these submerged landscapes with sonar and divers, and they have found stone tools and the remains of hearths beneath the seafloor. Such discoveries suggest that some early human settlements now lie underwater, which may explain gaps in the archaeological record on land.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the first two sentences in the text as a whole?","choices":["They explain why hearths were built near the sea.","They present a claim that the rest of the text disputes.","They describe the tools that archaeologists use.","They explain why land that people once lived on is now underwater."],"answer":"D","explanation":"Lower sea levels made now-submerged areas dry land. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.1cdeaf1608","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data4-69","passage":"<p class=\"src\">The following text is from a novel.</p><p>Every Saturday, Rafael's grandmother made tamales, and every Saturday she refused to write down the recipe. \"It's in my hands,\" she would say, holding them up, dusted with masa. So Rafael began standing beside her, watching how much she scooped, how long she kneaded, and how she folded each husk. Years later, in his own kitchen, he realized that the recipe had become his hands too.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the final sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It describes a disagreement between Rafael and his grandmother.","It reveals that Rafael has lost the recipe.","It shows that Rafael has absorbed the knowledge his grandmother described as being \"in my hands.\"","It explains why Rafael's grandmother refused to write down the recipe."],"answer":"C","explanation":"It echoes her words, showing the skill has passed to him. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.c18e3a522d","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data4-72","passage":"<p>Most spiders have eight eyes, but their eyesight varies widely. Web-building spiders often see poorly and sense prey mainly through vibrations in their silk. Jumping spiders, which hunt without webs, have large forward-facing eyes that give them some of the sharpest vision among small animals. This contrast suggests that a spider's hunting method is closely linked to how much it relies on sight.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?","choices":["It explains how spiders build webs step by step.","It notes that spiders' vision varies, contrasts two types of spiders, and draws a conclusion from the contrast.","It describes the life cycle of a single spider species.","It argues that spiders should be protected."],"answer":"B","explanation":"Variation, two contrasting examples, and a conclusion. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.51e8294ef9","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data4-75","passage":"<p>A company that makes running shoes gave one group of runners shoes with thick cushioning and another group shoes with minimal cushioning. After six months, the two groups reported similar rates of injury. However, runners in each group tended to change how their feet struck the ground: those in minimal shoes landed more lightly on the middle of the foot, while those in cushioned shoes more often landed on the heel. The researchers suggested that runners may adapt their stride to their shoes.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the third sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It contradicts the conclusion in the final sentence.","It describes how the shoes were manufactured.","It explains how injuries were measured.","It describes a difference between the groups that the injury data did not reveal."],"answer":"D","explanation":"\"However\" introduces differences in stride. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.584dc0d0b2","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data4-76","passage":"<p class=\"src\">The following text is from a short story.</p><p>For weeks, Mei had avoided the old man who sold newspapers outside the station, embarrassed by her halting attempts at the language. One morning she was a coin short. Before she could apologize, he waved his hand, pressed the paper into hers, and pointed at a headline, slowly pronouncing each word. She repeated them after him. The next morning, she stopped at his stand on purpose.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the final sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It describes the headline Mei read.","It explains why Mei was a coin short.","It shows that Mei's attitude toward the seller has changed.","It reveals that the seller has moved away."],"answer":"C","explanation":"She once avoided him but now seeks him out. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.5257e78481","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data4-77","passage":"<p>Scientists once thought that the deep ocean floor was nearly lifeless, too dark and cold to support much activity. Then researchers exploring volcanic vents discovered thriving communities of giant tube worms, clams, and shrimp. These animals depend not on sunlight but on bacteria that draw energy from chemicals released by the vents. The discovery showed that life can flourish in conditions once considered impossible.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?","choices":["It describes a debate that remains unresolved.","It lists the animals found in shallow reefs.","It describes an earlier belief, presents a discovery that contradicted it, and explains the discovery's significance.","It explains how volcanic vents form."],"answer":"C","explanation":"Old belief, vent discovery, and broader significance. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.98cfabc02e","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data4-79","passage":"<p>Some bird species are known to use the sun and stars to navigate, but a study of young songbirds raised indoors suggests that they may also inherit a sense of direction. Birds that had never migrated and had never seen the sky still became restless and tried to fly in the correct migratory direction at the right time of year. The researchers propose that young birds may be born with a rough compass that experience later refines.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the final sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It offers an interpretation of the behavior described in the previous sentence.","It explains how birds use the stars.","It contradicts the study's findings.","It describes how the birds were raised."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The inborn-compass idea explains the birds' orientation. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.f36fad3ada","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data4-80","passage":"<p class=\"src\">The following text is from a memoir.</p><p>My first job was washing dishes in a busy diner. I thought of it only as a way to earn money for a bicycle. But the cook, a woman named Dolores, noticed me watching her flip eggs and began teaching me during slow hours: how to crack an egg with one hand, how to tell by sound when the oil was hot. Thirty years and two restaurants later, I still crack eggs the way she taught me.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the second sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It explains how the narrator opened a restaurant.","It presents the narrator's limited view of the job, which later events change.","It suggests that the narrator disliked Dolores.","It describes Dolores's cooking techniques."],"answer":"B","explanation":"\"Only a way to earn money\" contrasts with what the job became. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.609bcb4840","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data4-85","passage":"<p>Paper was invented in China and spread gradually westward over many centuries. For much of that time, knowledge of papermaking was closely guarded. Historians note that papermaking reached new regions most often through trade routes and the movement of skilled workers, who brought their techniques with them. Once established, local paper mills made written records cheaper and far more common.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?","choices":["It compares paper with other writing materials.","It traces how a technology spread and then describes one effect of that spread.","It argues that paper should replace digital records.","It describes how paper is made step by step."],"answer":"B","explanation":"Spread of papermaking, then cheaper and more common records. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.eb0228062b","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data4-86","passage":"<p>Mangrove trees grow in salty coastal water, where most plants cannot survive. Some mangroves filter salt out at their roots, while others absorb salt and then push it out through their leaves, which can be seen coated with white crystals. Mangrove forests also protect shorelines by slowing waves with their dense, tangled roots.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the second sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It compares mangroves with desert plants.","It describes different ways mangroves deal with the salt mentioned in the first sentence.","It questions whether mangroves really live in salt water.","It explains why mangroves protect shorelines."],"answer":"B","explanation":"Filtering at roots or excreting through leaves. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.13fac5bcb4","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data4-90","passage":"<p>Some ancient Roman concrete structures, such as harbor walls, have survived in seawater for nearly two thousand years, while many modern concrete structures crack within decades. Researchers analyzing samples found that seawater seeping into the Roman concrete reacted with volcanic ash in the mixture, forming new minerals that filled cracks and made the material stronger over time.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?","choices":["It notes a striking difference in durability and then explains what researchers found about its cause.","It argues that modern concrete should never be used.","It lists famous Roman buildings.","It describes how the Romans built harbors."],"answer":"A","explanation":"Contrast in durability, then the mineral explanation. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.0d0889002f","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data4-91","passage":"<p>When a city library began lending musical instruments, librarians expected mostly children to borrow them. The most frequent borrowers turned out to be adults who had played instruments decades earlier and wanted to see whether they could still play. Several formed a small band that now rehearses in a library meeting room every Thursday evening.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the first sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It describes the band's first performance.","It states an expectation that the following sentences show was incorrect.","It lists the instruments available to borrow.","It explains how the library purchased instruments."],"answer":"B","explanation":"Librarians expected children; adults borrowed most. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.9a72f6e863","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data4-92","passage":"<p class=\"src\">The following text is adapted from a letter written by a young teacher in the early twentieth century.</p><p>The schoolhouse has one room, one stove, and twenty-three children between the ages of six and fifteen. I teach all of them at once. The older ones help the younger with their letters, and I have come to believe they learn as much by teaching as by listening to me. Yesterday a boy of twelve explained long division to a girl of eight more clearly than I could have.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the final sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It contradicts the teacher's earlier statement.","It explains why the teacher chose her profession.","It describes the schoolhouse's furnishings.","It gives an example supporting the teacher's belief about students learning by teaching."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The boy explaining division illustrates her point. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.81adb64476","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data4-93","passage":"<p>Scientists studying elephants noticed that the animals sometimes gathered and stood still, lifting a foot or leaning forward, even when no other elephants were visible. Recordings revealed that elephants produce very low-frequency rumbles that travel through the ground over long distances. Experiments suggested that elephants can detect these vibrations through sensitive nerve endings in their feet, which may explain the unusual postures.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?","choices":["It describes a puzzling behavior, presents findings about elephant communication, and offers an explanation for the behavior.","It compares elephants with other large mammals.","It describes an elephant herd's migration route.","It explains how scientists record animal sounds."],"answer":"A","explanation":"Puzzling postures, rumbles through the ground, and the foot-sensing explanation. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.62f6e9e49f","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data4-95","passage":"<p>Farmers in one region traditionally planted beans, corn, and squash together in the same field. Corn stalks give beans a structure to climb. Bean plants add nitrogen to the soil, which benefits the corn. Squash leaves spread across the ground, shading out weeds and helping the soil retain moisture. Each crop, in other words, helps the others grow.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the final sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It contradicts the details about squash.","It introduces a new crop.","It explains why the region is dry.","It summarizes the relationship illustrated by the preceding details."],"answer":"D","explanation":"\"In other words, helps the others grow.\" The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.edd3097c54","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data5-96","passage":"<p>When a remote island installed solar panels and batteries to replace its diesel generators, officials worried that cloudy weeks would leave residents without power. The system's designers addressed the concern by oversizing the battery bank and keeping one small generator for emergencies. In the first three years, the generator ran for a total of only eleven days, and the island's fuel costs fell by more than ninety percent.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the second sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It explains how the designers responded to the concern raised in the first sentence.","It presents evidence that the concern was justified.","It describes the island's geography.","It explains why diesel generators were installed originally."],"answer":"A","explanation":"Oversized batteries and a backup generator address cloudy weeks. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.b26abde461","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data5-98","passage":"<p>Ecologists studying a river noticed that trout populations were healthiest in stretches shaded by trees. Shade keeps water cooler, and cooler water holds more dissolved oxygen, which trout need. Where trees along the banks had been cleared for pasture, water temperatures rose in summer and trout numbers fell. Several landowners have since planted trees along the river to restore shade.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?","choices":["It argues that pastures should be eliminated.","It describes an observation, explains the reason behind it, gives supporting evidence, and notes a response.","It compares trout with other freshwater fish.","It describes how to plant trees along a riverbank."],"answer":"B","explanation":"Observation, cause, evidence from cleared areas, and replanting. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.274d531a46","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data5-100","passage":"<p>Some sea turtles nest on beaches lined with hotels and streetlights. Hatchlings typically find the ocean by crawling toward the brightest horizon, which on a natural beach is the moonlit sea. Artificial lights can lure them inland instead, where many die. Towns that require beachfront buildings to dim or shield their lights during nesting season have seen far more hatchlings reach the water.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the second sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It presents the results of dimming lights.","It describes how towns regulate hotel lighting.","It explains the natural behavior that artificial lights interfere with.","It explains why turtles nest near hotels."],"answer":"C","explanation":"Hatchlings crawl toward the brightest horizon. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.8f8ef3d498","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data5-103","passage":"<p>A company that designs video games tested two versions of a tutorial. In one, players read written instructions before starting. In the other, players learned controls gradually through short challenges during the first level. Players in the second group were more likely to finish the first level and to keep playing afterward. The company's designers concluded that people learn a game better by doing than by reading about it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the second and third sentences in the text as a whole?","choices":["They present the results of the test.","They describe the two versions being compared in the test.","They argue against the designers' conclusion.","They explain why the company makes video games."],"answer":"B","explanation":"One version uses reading, the other uses challenges. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.c9276ddeca","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data5-107","passage":"<p>Some cities have experimented with replacing traffic signals at busy intersections with roundabouts. At signals, cars sometimes speed through yellow lights, and the most dangerous crashes happen when vehicles collide at right angles. In roundabouts, all traffic moves in the same direction at lower speeds, so collisions that do occur tend to be glancing blows rather than direct hits. Studies of converted intersections have found large drops in serious injuries.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the second sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It presents the results of studies on roundabouts.","It argues that yellow lights should be longer.","It explains how roundabouts are designed.","It describes dangers at signaled intersections that roundabouts help avoid."],"answer":"D","explanation":"Speeding through yellow lights and right-angle crashes. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.1eee120631","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data5-108","passage":"<p>Honeybee colonies are sometimes described as \"superorganisms\" because individual bees function somewhat like cells in a body. Worker bees specialize in tasks such as foraging, nursing larvae, and guarding the entrance, and the colony as a whole regulates its own temperature. No single bee directs these activities; instead, they emerge from countless interactions among individuals responding to simple cues.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the final sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It describes the physical appearance of worker bees.","It explains how the colony's coordination occurs without a central leader.","It lists the tasks performed by worker bees.","It contradicts the comparison made in the first sentence."],"answer":"B","explanation":"Activities \"emerge from countless interactions.\" The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.6d45aa229e","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data5-110","passage":"<p class=\"src\">The following text is from a novel.</p><p>Wen had moved to the city expecting noise, crowds, and strangers who never looked at one another. What surprised her was the bakery on the corner. The owner learned her name on her second visit, set aside a sesame roll for her each morning, and asked about her new job as though they had known each other for years. By winter, the corner no longer felt like part of a strange city. It felt like her street.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the first sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It explains why Wen chose her new job.","It reveals the ending of the story.","It describes the bakery's location.","It presents Wen's expectations, which her experience at the bakery challenges."],"answer":"D","explanation":"She expected indifference but found personal attention. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.c98fcabca1","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data5-116","passage":"<p>When a public radio station began publishing transcripts of its programs online, some staff feared that people would read instead of listen, reducing the audience. Traffic data showed the opposite. Many readers who found transcripts through internet searches clicked to listen to the original broadcasts, and the station's online listening hours increased.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the sentence \"Traffic data showed the opposite\" in the text?","choices":["It signals that the evidence contradicted the staff's fear.","It indicates that the audience declined.","It explains why transcripts were published.","It describes how the station collected data."],"answer":"A","explanation":"Staff feared a decline; the data showed growth. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.b15950d6c4","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data5-118","passage":"<p>A city parks department noticed that its public benches were rarely used. Designers observed that most benches faced empty lawns or walls. They moved several benches to face walkways, playgrounds, and a fountain, where people could watch activity. Within weeks, the relocated benches were among the most used in the park, while those left in place remained mostly empty.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the final sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It describes how the benches were built.","It compares relocated benches with unmoved ones to show the change's effect.","It explains why the benches were originally placed facing walls.","It suggests that the relocation failed."],"answer":"B","explanation":"Moved benches were used; unmoved benches stayed empty. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.9931137a0f","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data5-119","passage":"<p class=\"src\">The following text is adapted from a nineteenth-century novel.</p><p>Mr. Ashworth prided himself on never changing his mind. He had decided at twenty that the new railway would ruin the countryside, and at seventy he still refused to ride it. When his granddaughter fell ill in the city, however, he was seen at the station before dawn, buying a ticket with shaking hands.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the first sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It explains why the granddaughter moved to the city.","It establishes a character trait that makes his final action significant.","It describes the railway's route.","It reveals that Mr. Ashworth is ill."],"answer":"B","explanation":"His pride in never changing his mind makes buying the ticket striking. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.2a0f8ff65a","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data5-120","passage":"<p>Beekeepers in one region reported that their honey tasted different from year to year. Chemists analyzing samples found that the flavor compounds in the honey closely matched the flowers that had bloomed most heavily each season. In years when wild thyme was abundant, for example, the honey contained compounds associated with thyme's distinctive flavor.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the final sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It provides a specific example of the pattern the chemists found.","It describes why thyme grows in the region.","It explains how honey is harvested.","It contradicts the beekeepers' observation."],"answer":"A","explanation":"Thyme years illustrate the flower-flavor link. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.69a7ebae22","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data6-125","passage":"<p class=\"src\">The following text is from a novel.</p><p>Grandfather had kept bees for fifty years, and he spoke to them every morning. \"Good morning, ladies,\" he would say, lifting the lid. My mother said it was nonsense. But the summer he was in the hospital and she tended the hives, I heard her through the kitchen window, standing by the boxes in her bathrobe, saying softly, \"Good morning, ladies. He'll be home soon.\"</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the sentence \"My mother said it was nonsense\" in the text?","choices":["It establishes the mother's earlier attitude, which contrasts with her later behavior.","It shows that the mother was afraid of bees.","It describes the hospital where the grandfather stayed.","It explains why the grandfather talked to the bees."],"answer":"A","explanation":"She calls it nonsense but later does it herself. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.29d561da54","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data6-129","passage":"<p class=\"src\">The following text is adapted from an essay.</p><p>We tend to think of maps as neutral pictures of the world, but every map involves choices. A mapmaker decides what to include and what to leave out, which places deserve large labels, and what to put at the center. A subway map that shows stations evenly spaced, for instance, is useful for riders precisely because it distorts real distances.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the final sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It contradicts the claim that maps involve choices.","It provides an example of a deliberate distortion that serves a purpose.","It explains how subway stations are built.","It describes the history of mapmaking."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The subway map illustrates purposeful choices. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.72c79d7603","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data6-130","passage":"<p>When a regional power company offered customers a discount for using less electricity during late afternoon peak hours, officials expected only a small response. Many households began running dishwashers and washing machines later in the evening instead. Peak demand fell enough that the company postponed building a new power plant it had planned.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?","choices":["It argues that dishwashers waste energy.","It compares power companies in two regions.","It explains how electricity is generated.","It describes an incentive, customers' responses, and a larger consequence."],"answer":"D","explanation":"Discount, behavior change, and a postponed plant. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.1c48bfa4ef","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data6-132","passage":"<p>Some libraries have eliminated late fees. Supporters argue that fees discourage low-income patrons, who may stop borrowing books rather than risk charges. One library system that removed fees found that many cardholders who had been blocked because of unpaid fines returned, and the rate at which books came back on time barely changed.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the second sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It argues that libraries should charge more.","It describes the results of eliminating fees.","It presents the reasoning of those who favor eliminating fees.","It explains how late fees are calculated."],"answer":"C","explanation":"Supporters argue fees discourage low-income patrons. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.ef4f2e3aec","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data6-133","passage":"<p class=\"src\">The following text is from a short story.</p><p>Ana had always hated her middle name, Esperanza, which the other kids pronounced wrong on purpose. At her grandmother's funeral, the priest explained that Esperanza meant \"hope,\" and that her grandmother had chosen it during a hard winter when the family had very little. Walking out of the church, Ana said the name quietly to herself, trying it out as if for the first time.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the first sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It reveals what the name means.","It explains why the grandmother chose the name.","It describes the funeral in detail.","It establishes Ana's negative feelings about her name, which later shift."],"answer":"D","explanation":"She \"had always hated\" it before learning its story. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.e34f790875","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data6-135","passage":"<p>In the nineteenth century, many people believed that tomatoes, a member of the nightshade family, were poisonous. Some nightshade plants are indeed toxic, and tomato leaves contain small amounts of harmful compounds. The fruit itself, however, is safe to eat. As more people cooked with tomatoes and suffered no ill effects, the fear faded, and tomatoes became a staple in many cuisines.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the second sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It proves that the belief was correct.","It explains why the belief described in the first sentence was understandable.","It describes how tomatoes are cooked.","It explains how tomatoes became popular."],"answer":"B","explanation":"Some relatives are toxic and the leaves contain harmful compounds. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.588514388c","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data6-136","passage":"<p>A company that manufactures outdoor jackets began offering free repairs for life. Executives worried that the program would reduce sales, since customers would buy fewer new jackets. Instead, sales rose. Surveys suggested that customers valued the promise that their jackets would last, and many chose the brand specifically because of the repair program.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the second sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It provides survey results.","It explains why the jackets are durable.","It describes how jackets are repaired.","It presents a concern that the outcome did not support."],"answer":"D","explanation":"Executives feared lower sales, but sales rose. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.3ab6495239","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data6-139","passage":"<p>For much of the twentieth century, doctors advised patients with back pain to rest in bed. Later studies found that patients who stayed active, within limits, often recovered faster than those who rested. Many guidelines now recommend gentle movement, such as walking, for most cases of short-term back pain.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?","choices":["It compares treatments for different illnesses.","It argues that doctors should stop treating back pain.","It describes the causes of back pain.","It describes earlier advice, presents research that challenged it, and states current recommendations."],"answer":"D","explanation":"Old advice, new studies, and current guidelines. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.778a6dd42a","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data6-144","passage":"<p>A study of online product reviews found that reviews rated as \"helpful\" by other shoppers tended to mention both positive and negative aspects of a product. Entirely positive reviews were rated helpful less often, perhaps because shoppers suspected them of being exaggerated or written by the seller.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the second sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It contrasts entirely positive reviews with balanced ones and suggests a reason for the difference.","It explains how the study was funded.","It argues that online reviews should be banned.","It describes how reviews are written."],"answer":"A","explanation":"Positive reviews were rated less helpful, possibly due to suspicion. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.aff5dc2646","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data6-146","passage":"<p class=\"src\">The following text is from a novel.</p><p>The new teacher did not take attendance by reading names. Instead, on the first morning, she asked each student to say one thing they had noticed on the way to school. The answers were slow at first: a red car, a barking dog. By Friday, students were describing the shape of clouds, the smell of rain on hot pavement, and the exact number of steps from the bus stop to the door.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?","choices":["It explains the rules for riding the school bus.","It describes the teacher's background and training.","It introduces a new routine and shows how students' responses develop over a week.","It compares two different schools."],"answer":"C","explanation":"First responses are simple; later ones are rich and precise. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.dc023af222","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data6-147","passage":"<p>Engineers designing a new stadium roof studied the structure of bird bones, which are hollow but reinforced with thin internal struts. The design allows bones to be light yet strong. Using a similar approach, the engineers created roof beams with hollow interiors crossed by thin supports, reducing the roof's weight by nearly a third without sacrificing strength.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the first two sentences in the text as a whole?","choices":["They describe the stadium's location.","They describe the natural design that inspired the engineers' solution.","They compare birds with other animals.","They explain why stadium roofs collapse."],"answer":"B","explanation":"Bird bone structure is the model. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.87217e6044","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data6-148","passage":"<p>A researcher studying how people choose where to sit in cafés found that most customers first selected seats along walls or near windows, leaving tables in the middle of the room empty until the café was crowded. The researcher suggests that people may prefer seats that offer a view while protecting their backs, a preference that may reflect a long-standing wariness of open spaces.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the second sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It explains how the researcher counted customers.","It describes the café's menu.","It offers an explanation for the seating pattern observed.","It contradicts the observation in the first sentence."],"answer":"C","explanation":"A view with a protected back. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.aa67ba2e5d","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data7-150","passage":"<p>When a university cafeteria stopped offering trays, officials hoped to save water used for washing them. They also found that food waste dropped by about a quarter. Without trays, students carried fewer dishes at once and tended to take only what they planned to eat, returning for seconds if they were still hungry.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the second sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It explains why trays were expensive.","It presents a drawback of removing trays.","It presents an additional, unexpected benefit of the change.","It describes how trays were washed."],"answer":"C","explanation":"The water-saving goal led to a second benefit. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.d74a2c2ef1","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data7-152","passage":"<p>Researchers studying sleep in dolphins found that the animals rest one half of their brain at a time while the other half stays alert. During this state, a dolphin keeps one eye open, surfaces regularly to breathe, and continues to watch for threats. After a period of time, the halves switch roles.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the second sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It describes activities dolphins can continue while half of the brain rests.","It argues that dolphins sleep less than other animals.","It describes the dolphins' diet.","It explains how researchers measured brain activity."],"answer":"A","explanation":"One eye open, surfacing, and watching for threats. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.da2bac64b0","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data7-153","passage":"<p>A city that installed sensors to monitor noise levels discovered that the loudest hours in one neighborhood were not late at night, as residents' complaints had suggested, but early in the morning, when delivery trucks unloaded at restaurants. Officials worked with businesses to shift deliveries to midday, and noise complaints fell.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?","choices":["It compares noise in several cities.","It argues that restaurants should close earlier.","It explains how noise sensors work.","It describes an unexpected finding and the action officials took in response."],"answer":"D","explanation":"Discovery about morning noise, then shifted deliveries. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.b0bbec2a15","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data7-154","passage":"<p>For years, scientists debated whether some dinosaurs cared for their young. Discoveries of fossilized nests changed the conversation. At one site, adult skeletons were found sitting on clutches of eggs in positions resembling those of brooding birds, suggesting that the adults were protecting or warming the eggs when they died.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the final sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It explains why scientists stopped studying dinosaurs.","It contradicts the first sentence.","It describes evidence that supports the idea of parental care.","It describes how fossils form."],"answer":"C","explanation":"Adults found sitting on eggs. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.947582f0c4","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data7-155","passage":"<p class=\"src\">The following text is adapted from an essay.</p><p>The first time I saw the ocean, I was sixteen and disappointed. I had imagined something like the postcards: impossible blue, gentle waves. The real ocean that day was gray and loud and cold, and it smelled of salt and seaweed. It took me years to understand that I had not been disappointed by the ocean. I had been disappointed by the postcards.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the final sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It shows that the writer never returned to the ocean.","It describes the weather on the day of the visit.","It reframes the writer's early disappointment by identifying its true source.","It explains why the writer bought postcards."],"answer":"C","explanation":"The disappointment was with the postcards. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.1694d4a618","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data7-156","passage":"<p>When a school introduced a program in which students grew vegetables in a garden and then cooked them in class, researchers surveyed students' eating habits before and after. Students in the program reported eating more vegetables at home, and many said they were more willing to try unfamiliar foods. Students at a similar school without the program showed no such change.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the final sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It suggests that the program had no effect.","It describes the vegetables grown in the garden.","It explains why the program was created.","It provides a comparison that strengthens the link between the program and the changes."],"answer":"D","explanation":"No change at the comparison school. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.24bf84b29b","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data7-157","passage":"<p>Ancient Polynesian navigators crossed vast stretches of the Pacific without instruments. They read the positions of stars, the direction and shape of ocean swells, and the flight paths of seabirds, which head out to sea in the morning and return to land at dusk. By combining these clues, navigators could locate islands far beyond the horizon.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the second sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It lists the natural clues navigators used.","It explains why Polynesians began voyaging.","It contradicts the first sentence.","It describes the construction of canoes."],"answer":"A","explanation":"Stars, swells, and seabirds. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.a2a7329406","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data7-158","passage":"<p>Researchers found that people shopping online tend to buy more when a website shows how many other people have recently purchased an item. When the counter was removed from one site, sales of those items fell modestly. The researchers suggest that people use others' choices as a shortcut when they are uncertain about what to buy.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the second sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It describes how items are shipped.","It provides evidence supporting the pattern described in the first sentence.","It suggests that counters have no effect.","It explains why websites add counters."],"answer":"B","explanation":"Removing the counter reduced sales. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.ab0b45f69c","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data7-161","passage":"<p>Early astronomers noticed that the planet Mars sometimes appeared to move backward across the sky for several weeks before resuming its usual direction. Some explained this with complex systems of circles within circles. The motion is now understood as an effect of perspective: Earth, moving faster in its orbit, periodically overtakes Mars, making Mars appear to slip backward.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?","choices":["It describes a puzzling observation, an early explanation, and the modern explanation.","It describes how telescopes work.","It argues that early astronomers were correct.","It compares Mars and Venus."],"answer":"A","explanation":"Observation, circles within circles, and perspective. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.c36d35e6b2","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data7-162","passage":"<p>When a museum added benches to its galleries, curators noticed that visitors spent more time looking at individual artworks. Before, most people walked past paintings quickly while standing. With a place to sit, visitors often stayed in front of a single piece for several minutes, and some reported noticing details they would otherwise have missed.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the second sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It describes the museum's most famous painting.","It describes visitors' behavior before the change, for comparison.","It explains how the benches were designed.","It argues that museums should remove paintings."],"answer":"B","explanation":"Walking past quickly contrasts with sitting and looking. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.b7fa1222ba","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data7-163","passage":"<p>Salmon that hatch in rivers spend years in the ocean before returning to spawn. When they die after spawning, their bodies decompose along riverbanks. Scientists have found traces of ocean nitrogen in streamside trees, delivered by salmon carcasses dragged into the forest by bears. The fish, in effect, carry nutrients from the sea into the forest.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the final sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It explains how bears catch salmon.","It contradicts the evidence about nitrogen.","It introduces a new animal.","It summarizes the significance of the process described."],"answer":"D","explanation":"Salmon carry sea nutrients into the forest. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.ae63ec58d2","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data7-164","passage":"<p class=\"src\">The following text is from a memoir.</p><p>My grandmother never threw anything away. Jars held buttons, rubber bands, and bits of string. As a teenager I found this embarrassing. Then, during a week-long power outage, our neighbors came to her door one by one, asking for candles, batteries, a length of wire, a spare key. She had everything. She handed it all over with a small, satisfied smile.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the sentence \"As a teenager I found this embarrassing\" in the text?","choices":["It presents the narrator's earlier attitude, which the later events challenge.","It shows the neighbors' opinion of the grandmother.","It explains why the grandmother saved items.","It describes the power outage."],"answer":"A","explanation":"Embarrassment gives way to appreciation. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.d4f1634053","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data7-166","passage":"<p>Linguists recording conversations noticed that speakers often pause briefly before important or unexpected words. Listeners, in experiments, were better at remembering words that followed such pauses. The researchers suggest that pauses may help listeners by signaling that something worth attention is coming.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the final sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It describes how conversations were recorded.","It lists the words used in the experiment.","It offers an explanation for the findings described earlier.","It contradicts the experimental results."],"answer":"C","explanation":"Pauses may signal importance. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.254ecac8ef","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data7-167","passage":"<p>For decades, a small town's annual fair featured a pie contest judged by the same three residents. When the organizers began inviting judges from neighboring towns, several longtime participants worried that outsiders would not appreciate local recipes. Instead, entries increased, and a pie made with a rarely used local fruit won first prize for the first time, drawing new attention to the fruit.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the second sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It presents a worry that the outcome described in the final sentence did not support.","It explains why the fair was founded.","It describes the pies entered in the contest.","It lists the judges' names."],"answer":"A","explanation":"Fears about outsiders were not borne out. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.a169b63c60","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data7-168","passage":"<p>Scientists studying why zebras have stripes tested several ideas. When horses wore striped coats, biting flies landed on them far less often than on horses wearing solid-colored coats, although flies still approached. The researchers suggest that stripes may confuse flies as they try to land, which could help zebras avoid insect-borne diseases.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the phrase \"although flies still approached\" in the text?","choices":["It suggests that flies prefer solid colors.","It shows that the experiment failed.","It explains how the coats were made.","It clarifies that stripes interfered with landing rather than keeping flies away entirely."],"answer":"D","explanation":"Flies came near but struggled to land. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.9783208444","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data7-171","passage":"<p>Researchers studying how people read food labels used eye-tracking devices and found that most shoppers looked at the calorie count and the price but rarely read the ingredient list. When the ingredient list was moved to the front of the package and printed in larger type, shoppers were far more likely to read it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?","choices":["It argues that calorie counts should be removed.","It describes a pattern in shoppers' behavior and then a change that altered it.","It compares the prices of several foods.","It explains how eye-tracking devices are built."],"answer":"B","explanation":"Rarely read lists, then prominent lists read more. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.9b82bb5ee1","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data7-173","passage":"<p>When a regional newspaper began publishing weekly articles written by high school students about their communities, editors expected little interest from adult readers. Instead, the student articles were among the most read on the paper's website, and several local officials cited them at public meetings as helpful views of issues they had overlooked.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the first clause, \"editors expected little interest from adult readers,\" in the text?","choices":["It describes the newspaper's history.","It explains why students wrote the articles.","It summarizes officials' reactions.","It establishes an expectation that the results contradicted."],"answer":"D","explanation":"Low expectations contrast with high readership. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.eee0d002e6","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data7-175","passage":"<p class=\"src\">The following text is from a novel.</p><p>Marco had lived above the bakery for ten years and had long since stopped noticing the smell of bread. Then he spent a month traveling for work. On the night he returned, he climbed the stairs, opened his door, and stopped, overwhelmed by the warm scent of yeast and butter drifting up through the floorboards, as though the building itself were welcoming him home.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the first sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It establishes that Marco had grown used to the smell, which makes his later reaction meaningful.","It explains why Marco traveled for work.","It reveals that Marco owns the bakery.","It describes the bakery's menu."],"answer":"A","explanation":"He \"had long since stopped noticing\" the smell. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.c3d0b8fe99","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data8-177","passage":"<p>When a city began offering free swimming lessons to children in neighborhoods without public pools, officials bused students to a recreation center across town. Participation was lower than expected. Surveys found that many families could not accommodate the long bus rides after school. The city then set up temporary pools at neighborhood schools during the summer, and enrollment tripled.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?","choices":["It compares swimming with other sports.","It explains how temporary pools are built.","It describes a program, a problem with participation and its cause, and a change that addressed it.","It argues that swimming lessons should cost money."],"answer":"C","explanation":"Low participation, survey findings, and relocation. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.5c4e3a2401","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data8-186","passage":"<p>A school district that shortened its summer break and added more short breaks throughout the year hoped to reduce learning loss. Teachers reported spending less time reviewing material in the fall. Some families, however, struggled to find child care during the new breaks, which did not align with the schedules of nearby districts.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the final sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It describes the length of the new breaks.","It explains why the district adopted the change.","It presents a drawback of the change.","It supports the teachers' reports."],"answer":"C","explanation":"Child care problems. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.48af848aed","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data8-188","passage":"<p>Biologists studying hibernating ground squirrels found that the animals periodically warm themselves up during hibernation, raising their body temperature for about a day before cooling down again. These arousals use a large share of the energy the squirrels spend over the winter. Researchers suspect the arousals may be necessary for functions such as sleep or immune activity that cannot occur at very low body temperatures.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the second sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It highlights the energy cost of the arousals, making their purpose puzzling.","It proves that arousals are unnecessary.","It describes the squirrels' burrows.","It explains how squirrels find food."],"answer":"A","explanation":"A large energy share raises the question of why they occur. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.9b2f8052b4","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data8-190","passage":"<p>Scientists examining ice cores from Greenland found layers of dust and chemicals that correspond to large volcanic eruptions. By counting annual layers of snow, much like tree rings, researchers could date the eruptions and compare them with historical records of cold summers and poor harvests. Several recorded famines coincided with volcanic layers in the ice.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?","choices":["It explains how volcanoes form.","It argues that famines are caused only by wars.","It describes what ice cores contain, how they were dated, and what the comparison with historical records revealed.","It compares Greenland and Antarctica."],"answer":"C","explanation":"Contents, dating method, and findings. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.37bcb4844f","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data8-191","passage":"<p>When a small town's only doctor retired, residents feared they would lose local medical care. The town partnered with a nearby hospital to set up video appointments at the library, staffed by a nurse who could take measurements during calls. Many residents were initially skeptical, but within a year most routine visits happened this way, and patients reported saving hours of travel.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the phrase \"Many residents were initially skeptical\" in the text?","choices":["It indicates early doubts that were later overcome.","It shows that the program failed.","It explains why the doctor retired.","It describes the nurse's training."],"answer":"A","explanation":"Skepticism gave way to widespread use. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.530452887c","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data8-193","passage":"<p class=\"src\">The following text is from a poem.</p><p>The river does not remember / the mountain it came from, / nor does it know the ocean / where it will someday run. / It only knows the stones it turns / and the reeds along its way, / and it sings to them the one song / it has: today, today.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the overall structure of the poem?","choices":["It narrates a journey from the ocean to the mountain.","It compares two rivers.","It describes what the river does not know and then what it does know.","It describes a storm and its aftermath."],"answer":"C","explanation":"Past and future unknown, present known. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.5121aa48fa","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data8-194","passage":"<p>Engineers testing self-driving cars found that the vehicles handled highway driving well but struggled in situations requiring interpretation of human behavior, such as a pedestrian waving a driver forward or a cyclist making eye contact before turning. Human drivers rely on such informal signals, which are difficult to program.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the second sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It describes how highways are built.","It argues that cyclists should not make eye contact.","It presents the results of highway tests.","It explains why the situations described earlier are challenging for self-driving cars."],"answer":"D","explanation":"Informal signals \"are difficult to program.\" The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.60c0bea484","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data8-196","passage":"<p>When a library replaced its self-checkout machines with staffed desks for a trial period, checkout times increased slightly. Surveys, however, showed that patrons asked librarians many more questions, often about finding books, using databases, or getting help with job applications. Several patrons said they had not realized librarians could help with such tasks.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the word \"however\" in the text?","choices":["It indicates that the trial failed.","It signals a benefit that offsets the slight increase in checkout time.","It introduces the library's history.","It explains how machines work."],"answer":"B","explanation":"Slower checkout, but more assistance. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.61792732f9","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data9-197","passage":"<p>When a coastal city's fishing industry declined, many old wooden boats were left to rot in the harbor. A group of retired shipwrights began restoring a few of them and offering free sailing lessons to local teenagers. The project grew into a program that now teaches boatbuilding skills, and several graduates have found jobs at repair yards along the coast.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?","choices":["It compares fishing and sailing.","It explains how wooden boats are built step by step.","It argues that harbors should be closed.","It describes a situation of decline, a response to it, and how that response developed."],"answer":"D","explanation":"Decline, restoration and lessons, and growth into job training. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.4985f0d6ac","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data9-199","passage":"<p>Researchers who installed underwater microphones near a restored oyster reef found that the reef grew noisier over several years, filled with the clicks and grunts of fish and shrimp. The noise levels closely tracked increases in the numbers of animals divers counted. The researchers suggest that recording sound could offer a cheaper way to monitor reef recovery than frequent diving surveys.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the second sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It argues that divers are unnecessary.","It shows that the recorded sound corresponded to actual changes in animal numbers.","It describes the types of oysters on the reef.","It explains how microphones are waterproofed."],"answer":"B","explanation":"Noise \"closely tracked\" counts. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.50fe2df6a7","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data9-200","passage":"<p>In the early twentieth century, many cities replaced horse-drawn carriages with automobiles, partly to solve a pollution problem: horse manure filled streets, attracting flies and spreading disease. Cars eliminated that problem but introduced new ones, including exhaust fumes and traffic accidents, that later generations would struggle to address.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the word \"but\" in the second sentence?","choices":["It shows that cars failed to reduce manure.","It describes the benefits of horses.","It introduces the drawbacks that followed the solution.","It explains why horses were used."],"answer":"C","explanation":"\"Eliminated that problem but introduced new ones.\" The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.511ece209c","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data9-202","passage":"<p>When scientists studied honey found in ancient tombs, they discovered that some of it was still edible after thousands of years. Honey's low water content and high acidity make it inhospitable to bacteria, and bees add an enzyme that produces small amounts of hydrogen peroxide, which further prevents spoilage.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the second sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It explains the properties that account for the discovery described in the first sentence.","It explains how bees collect nectar.","It questions whether the honey was really edible.","It describes how tombs were built."],"answer":"A","explanation":"Low water, acidity, and hydrogen peroxide. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.833c657c2d","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data9-206","passage":"<p>When an airline began allowing passengers to board from both the front and back doors of the plane, the average boarding time dropped by several minutes. Crowding in the aisle decreased because passengers seated near the rear no longer had to squeeze past those stowing bags in front rows.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the second sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It explains why boarding time decreased.","It explains how bags are stowed.","It describes the airline's routes.","It presents a drawback of the change."],"answer":"A","explanation":"Less aisle crowding. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.5c1c92f612","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data9-207","passage":"<p>Some trees in dense forests grow tall and thin, while trees of the same species growing in open fields spread wide branches and remain shorter. In a crowded forest, sunlight is limited at lower levels, so growing upward quickly helps a tree reach light. In an open field, sunlight is available all around, and wide branches can capture it efficiently.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the second and third sentences in the text as a whole?","choices":["They compare trees with shrubs.","They explain the difference in tree shape described in the first sentence.","They describe how forests are planted.","They contradict the first sentence."],"answer":"B","explanation":"Light conditions explain the shapes. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.46fecddc27","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data9-210","passage":"<p>When a company introduced a policy allowing employees to work any hours they chose as long as they completed their tasks, managers worried that collaboration would suffer. Communication did become harder at first. Teams responded by agreeing on a few core hours when everyone would be available, and surveys later showed high satisfaction with the flexible schedule.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?","choices":["It argues against flexible schedules.","It explains how to write surveys.","It compares two companies.","It describes a policy, an initial problem, the solution teams developed, and the outcome."],"answer":"D","explanation":"Policy, difficulty, core hours, and satisfaction. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.34dcc7b89e","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data9-211","passage":"<p>Biologists noticed that some species of butterfly that are harmless to birds closely resemble species that taste bitter or are toxic. Birds that have learned to avoid the toxic butterflies also tend to avoid the harmless look-alikes. The resemblance, researchers suggest, protects the harmless species even though it has no defenses of its own.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the second sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It contradicts the first sentence.","It explains how butterflies become toxic.","It describes the butterflies' migration.","It explains how the resemblance benefits the harmless butterflies."],"answer":"D","explanation":"Birds avoid look-alikes. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.ec87dfd8ff","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data9-213","passage":"<p>When a bakery began selling day-old bread at half price, the owner expected sales of fresh bread to fall. Instead, fresh bread sales held steady, and the discounted bread attracted new customers, some of whom later bought fresh items. Food waste at the bakery also dropped.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the first sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It explains why bread becomes stale.","It states an expectation that the results did not support.","It lists the bakery's products.","It describes how bread is baked."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The owner expected lower fresh sales. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.a934e846f6","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data9-214","passage":"<p class=\"src\">The following text is from a poem.</p><p>I kept my grandmother's thimble / in a drawer for twenty years, / a silver cap too small / for any finger but her own. / Tonight I sewed a button / on my daughter's winter coat, / and without thinking, / I slipped the thimble on.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the overall structure of the poem?","choices":["It compares two coats.","It describes a long-kept object and then a moment when the speaker uses it.","It lists items in a drawer.","It describes a winter storm."],"answer":"B","explanation":"Kept for twenty years, then used. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.0c8e0eaa19","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data9-215","passage":"<p>A city testing electric buses found that they cost more to buy than diesel buses but less to fuel and maintain. Over a bus's expected lifetime, the total costs were roughly equal. The electric buses also reduced noise and exhaust along routes through dense neighborhoods, which residents reported appreciating.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the final sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It shows that electric buses were more expensive overall.","It describes the bus routes.","It describes benefits beyond cost considerations.","It explains how electric buses are charged."],"answer":"C","explanation":"Reduced noise and exhaust. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.a828517e8d","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data10-218","passage":"<p>Researchers studying rats found that animals given access to running wheels learned their way through mazes faster than rats without wheels. The exercising rats also showed more new neuron growth in a brain region associated with memory. The researchers caution that rats differ from humans but suggest that exercise may support learning in other animals as well.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the final sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It acknowledges a limitation while suggesting a broader implication.","It describes how the mazes were built.","It explains why rats like running wheels.","It contradicts the findings about neurons."],"answer":"A","explanation":"Caution about rats versus humans. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.9ed6e86015","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data10-220","passage":"<p>Some caves contain formations called stalactites, which hang from ceilings like icicles. They form over thousands of years as water dripping from the ceiling leaves behind tiny amounts of dissolved minerals. Because they grow so slowly, scientists can analyze their layers to learn about past rainfall and climate in the region.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the final sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It explains a scientific use that follows from how stalactites form.","It explains why caves are dark.","It describes the appearance of stalactites.","It questions how stalactites form."],"answer":"A","explanation":"Slow growth allows climate analysis. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.4ebd678479","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data10-223","passage":"<p>Scientists studying a mountain lake found that its water had become clearer over several decades. At first they suspected reduced pollution. Further investigation showed that an invasive species of mussel, which filters tiny particles from the water, had spread throughout the lake. The mussels made the water clearer but also removed plankton that native fish depend on for food.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?","choices":["It explains how mussels reproduce.","It compares two lakes.","It argues that lakes should be drained.","It describes a change, an initial explanation, the actual cause, and that cause's negative effect."],"answer":"D","explanation":"Clearer water, suspected cause, mussels, and harm to fish. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.79b554e6a3","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data10-224","passage":"<p>Some schools have introduced \"reading buddies\" programs in which older students read with younger ones. Teachers in one school reported that younger children's reading improved, as expected. They were surprised to find that many older students who struggled with reading also showed gains, perhaps because reading aloud to younger children gave them low-pressure practice.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the final sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It explains why younger children struggle.","It describes how buddies were paired.","It restates the expected result.","It presents an unexpected benefit and a possible reason for it."],"answer":"D","explanation":"Surprising gains with an explanation. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.67917c5c47","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data10-225","passage":"<p class=\"src\">The following text is from a poem.</p><p>The lamp in the window of the corner store / has burned each night for forty years. / Travelers who have never met the owner / measure their journeys by its light, / and though it saves no lives, / it tells them, turning the last corner, / that someone, somewhere on this street, / is still awake.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the phrase \"though it saves no lives\" in the poem?","choices":["It explains how the lamp is powered.","It suggests that the lamp is dangerous.","It describes the owner's job.","It acknowledges the lamp's modest practical importance before emphasizing its emotional value."],"answer":"D","explanation":"Modest role, but meaningful comfort. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.9d090d22af","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data10-226","passage":"<p>Engineers testing a new type of road surface made of porous pavement found that rainwater drained through it rather than running off. During storms, streets with the new surface had less standing water, and nearby storm drains overflowed less often. In cold regions, however, water trapped in the pavement could freeze and damage it, requiring more maintenance.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the final sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It explains the benefits of the pavement.","It presents a limitation of the pavement in certain conditions.","It describes storm drains.","It describes how the pavement is manufactured."],"answer":"B","explanation":"Freezing water can damage it. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.2dbb6ca664","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data10-228","passage":"<p>For many years, cities built public housing as large, isolated high-rise complexes. Critics later argued that concentrating many low-income families in one place limited access to jobs and services. More recent programs have favored mixed-income developments spread throughout neighborhoods, which some studies suggest can improve residents' access to opportunities.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?","choices":["It describes an earlier approach, criticism of it, and a newer approach.","It compares housing prices in two cities.","It describes the architecture of one building.","It argues that public housing should end."],"answer":"A","explanation":"Old model, critique, new model. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.c364639877","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data11-235","passage":"<p>Some desert beetles collect drinking water from fog. The beetles stand on sand dunes with their backs tilted into the wind, and tiny droplets of fog collect on bumps on their shells, eventually rolling down into their mouths. Engineers have studied the beetles' shells to design surfaces that harvest water from fog in dry regions.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the final sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It explains why fog forms.","It describes a human application inspired by the beetles' behavior.","It questions whether beetles drink fog.","It describes beetles' predators."],"answer":"B","explanation":"Engineers imitate the shell design. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.d75c1cde0d","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data11-236","passage":"<p class=\"src\">The following text is from a memoir.</p><p>I spent the summer I was fourteen working at my aunt's flower shop, convinced it would be the dullest job imaginable. By August I knew the names of forty flowers, could tie a bow with my eyes closed, and had watched a nervous young man spend twenty minutes choosing roses for a proposal. I had expected to count the days. Instead, I counted the stories.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the final two sentences in the text as a whole?","choices":["They describe how to tie a bow.","They list the flowers sold in the shop.","They contrast the narrator's expectation with her actual experience.","They explain why the young man chose roses."],"answer":"C","explanation":"Counting days versus counting stories. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.82c4bc1aff","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data11-238","passage":"<p>For centuries, farmers in some mountain regions have raised a breed of sheep with unusually thick wool that allows the animals to survive harsh winters. As many farmers switched to faster-growing breeds, the traditional sheep became rare. Recently, some weavers have begun paying premium prices for its wool, prized for its warmth and durability, giving farmers a reason to keep raising the breed.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?","choices":["It explains how wool is spun into yarn.","It compares sheep with goats.","It describes a traditional breed, its decline, and a development that may help it survive.","It argues that farmers should stop raising sheep."],"answer":"C","explanation":"Tradition, decline, and renewed demand. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.d2065a14d0","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data11-240","passage":"<p>Many octopus species live only a year or two and die soon after reproducing. Female octopuses guard their eggs without eating, sometimes for months, until the eggs hatch. Researchers have found that a gland near the octopus's eyes triggers changes that lead to this fasting and decline; when the gland was removed in experiments, mothers abandoned their eggs, resumed eating, and lived longer.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the final sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It explains why octopuses change color.","It describes where octopuses lay eggs.","It contradicts the claim that octopuses guard eggs.","It presents experimental evidence identifying a cause of the behavior described earlier."],"answer":"D","explanation":"Removing the gland changed behavior. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.43d16724b8","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data11-243","passage":"<p class=\"src\">The following text is from a short story.</p><p>For the whole bus ride, the new girl sat alone, staring out the window. Rosa had planned to sit with her friends, as always. But when the bus stopped at the school, Rosa noticed the girl clutching a map of the building, her hands trembling slightly. Rosa slid into the seat beside her and asked, \"Want me to show you where the gym is?\"</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the sentence \"Rosa had planned to sit with her friends, as always\" in the text?","choices":["It shows that Rosa's decision to help involves changing her routine.","It reveals that Rosa has no friends.","It describes the bus route.","It explains why the new girl sat alone."],"answer":"A","explanation":"Helping means breaking from habit. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.45f5d4a6ae","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data11-244","passage":"<p>When a coastal town prohibited single-use plastic bags, many shoppers switched to reusable bags. Litter surveys found far fewer plastic bags on beaches afterward. Sales of small plastic trash bags, however, increased, as some residents had previously reused shopping bags to line household wastebaskets.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the final sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It describes an unintended effect of the ban.","It supports the claim that litter decreased.","It describes how beaches are cleaned.","It explains why reusable bags are popular."],"answer":"A","explanation":"Trash bag sales rose. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.aa99873636","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data11-245","passage":"<p>Scientists studying why some leaves change color in autumn found that as days shorten, trees stop producing green chlorophyll, revealing yellow and orange pigments already present in the leaves. Red colors, however, come from pigments that some trees actively produce in autumn, possibly to protect leaves from sun damage while the trees reabsorb nutrients before the leaves fall.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the word \"however\" in the text?","choices":["It indicates that leaves stay green.","It introduces a contradiction about chlorophyll.","It shows that the study failed.","It signals that red colors have a different origin than yellow and orange."],"answer":"D","explanation":"Red comes from actively produced pigments. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.4d5203f295","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data11-248","passage":"<p>Researchers analyzing thousands of hours of basketball games found that teams attempting more three-point shots scored more points per possession on average, even though three-pointers are made less often than shorter shots. Because each successful three-pointer earns an extra point, the higher reward can outweigh the lower success rate. The finding helped explain why many teams increased their three-point attempts.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the second sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It contradicts the first sentence.","It describes the size of basketball courts.","It explains how three-pointers can be more valuable despite being missed more often.","It describes the history of the three-point line."],"answer":"C","explanation":"The extra point outweighs the lower success rate. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.8a6c31eeef","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data11-249","passage":"<p>When a museum began offering sensory-friendly hours, with dimmed lights, quieter galleries, and limited crowds, officials expected to serve mainly visitors with autism. Attendance data showed that many older adults and parents with young children also chose these hours, preferring the calmer atmosphere.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the second sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It contradicts the purpose of the program.","It shows that the program's appeal extended beyond its intended audience.","It explains how lights were dimmed.","It describes the museum's exhibits."],"answer":"B","explanation":"Older adults and parents also attended. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.603bda3205","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data11-250","passage":"<p>Geologists studying a river canyon noticed that some of the rock layers exposed in its walls contain fossils of marine animals, even though the canyon lies far inland and high above sea level. The fossils indicate that the region was once covered by a shallow sea before geological forces lifted the land.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the phrase \"even though the canyon lies far inland and high above sea level\" in the text?","choices":["It highlights why the fossils' presence is surprising.","It explains how rivers form canyons.","It describes the canyon's width.","It suggests the fossils are fake."],"answer":"A","explanation":"Marine fossils inland need explanation. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.e5acedb84c","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data11-251","passage":"<p>When a public radio station invited listeners to submit short audio stories about their neighborhoods, producers expected a few dozen entries. They received more than a thousand. Many stories came from people who had never spoken on the radio before, and several became among the station's most shared segments online.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the sentence \"They received more than a thousand\" in the text?","choices":["It shows that the project failed.","It emphasizes how greatly the response exceeded expectations.","It explains how stories were recorded.","It describes the neighborhoods."],"answer":"B","explanation":"A few dozen expected versus more than a thousand. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.eb4fdcbc57","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data11-253","passage":"<p class=\"src\">The following text is from a novel.</p><p>Every year on the first snowfall, Grandmother Ana made hot chocolate and told the same story about the winter she met Grandfather. The grandchildren could recite it word for word and pretended to groan. But the year Grandmother was too ill to tell it, the youngest, Pilar, stood up in front of the fire, took a deep breath, and began: \"It was the coldest winter anyone could remember...\"</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the sentence \"The grandchildren could recite it word for word and pretended to groan\" in the text?","choices":["It shows that the children disliked their grandmother.","It explains why the grandmother became ill.","It describes the hot chocolate recipe.","It shows that the tradition was familiar and more beloved than the children let on."],"answer":"D","explanation":"Their \"pretended\" groans hide affection. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.c695d60e18","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data12-257","passage":"<p>When a regional airline started posting its on-time performance for each route on its website, some routes with poor records improved within months. Managers reported that public comparison motivated staff to find solutions, such as adjusting schedules that had been unrealistic and positioning spare parts at busy airports.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the second sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It explains how staff improved the routes' performance.","It lists every route the airline flies.","It describes the airline's history.","It shows that posting data had no effect."],"answer":"A","explanation":"Adjusted schedules and positioned parts. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.5b5f865c98","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data12-258","passage":"<p>Some species of fireflies synchronize their flashing, so that thousands of insects in a forest blink at nearly the same moment. Researchers suggest that synchronized flashing may help females recognize males of their own species amid the visual clutter of many flashing insects. Experiments with artificial lights showed that females responded more often to synchronized flashes than to random ones.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the final sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It contradicts the researchers' suggestion.","It describes the forest where fireflies live.","It presents evidence supporting the explanation offered in the second sentence.","It explains how artificial lights are made."],"answer":"C","explanation":"Females responded more to synchronized flashes. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.bce66d362e","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data12-260","passage":"<p>A study tracking two groups of patients recovering from knee surgery found that those who began gentle physical therapy within a day of surgery regained mobility faster than those who waited a week. Patients who started early also reported less stiffness. The researchers cautioned that the early therapy must be carefully supervised to avoid injury.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the final sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It adds a caution about how the findings should be applied.","It describes the surgery in detail.","It contradicts the finding about mobility.","It explains why patients had surgery."],"answer":"A","explanation":"Therapy must be supervised. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.8443fb467d","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data12-264","passage":"<p>Many cities have begun converting parking spaces into small outdoor seating areas called parklets. In one city, businesses next to parklets reported increased foot traffic and sales, though some drivers complained about losing parking. A survey found that most customers of those businesses arrived on foot, by bike, or by transit rather than by car.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the final sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It explains why cities have parking spaces.","It provides information that helps explain why losing parking did not hurt businesses.","It supports the drivers' complaints.","It describes how parklets are built."],"answer":"B","explanation":"Most customers didn't drive. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.2ec8f1906d","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data12-269","passage":"<p>Researchers studying ancient wheat found that farmers thousands of years ago gradually selected plants whose seed heads did not shatter and scatter seeds on the ground. Wild wheat drops its seeds when ripe, which helps it spread, but that trait made harvesting difficult. By saving seeds from plants that held onto their grain, early farmers changed the crop over generations.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the second sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It contradicts the first sentence.","It explains how bread is made.","It explains why the trait farmers selected against was useful in the wild but a problem for harvesting.","It describes modern wheat farming."],"answer":"C","explanation":"Scattering aids spread but hinders harvest. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.601994b645","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data12-270","passage":"<p>A study of children's playgrounds found that equipment with some element of manageable risk, such as higher climbing structures, kept children engaged longer than very low, simple equipment. Injury rates were similar between the two types of playgrounds. Researchers suggest that appropriate challenges help children build confidence and physical skills.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the second sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It describes how playgrounds are designed.","It explains why children like simple equipment.","It addresses a likely concern about more challenging equipment.","It contradicts the finding about engagement."],"answer":"C","explanation":"Injury rates were similar. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.735981eeb7","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data13-272","passage":"<p class=\"src\">The following text is from a novel.</p><p>Grandfather's toolbox had sat in the garage untouched since his funeral. When the porch step cracked, Esteban's mother reached for her phone to call a carpenter. Esteban stopped her. He opened the toolbox, found the hammer with the tape-wrapped handle, and felt his fingers settle into the worn places where his grandfather's had been.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the first sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It reveals Esteban's age.","It describes the carpenter's prices.","It explains how the porch step cracked.","It establishes the toolbox's connection to the grandfather's absence."],"answer":"D","explanation":"Untouched since the funeral. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.27cb803ee7","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data13-273","passage":"<p>Biologists found that some trees in dry regions shed their leaves during drought and quickly regrow them after rain, while other trees keep their leaves but close tiny pores to conserve water. Trees that drop their leaves avoid water loss almost entirely but cannot produce food until they regrow leaves. Trees that keep leaves can resume food production immediately but still lose some water.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?","choices":["It argues that one strategy is always better.","It compares trees with shrubs.","It introduces two strategies and then describes an advantage and disadvantage of each.","It explains how rain forms."],"answer":"C","explanation":"Leaf-dropping versus pore-closing trade-offs. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.f660b89cdf","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data13-276","passage":"<p class=\"src\">The following text is from a memoir.</p><p>I learned patience from my grandmother's bread. She would mix the dough and then do nothing at all for two hours, reading or knitting while it rose. As a child I found this unbearable and would lift the towel every ten minutes to check. \"Watching doesn't make it grow faster,\" she'd say, and pull the towel back down.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the first sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It states the lesson that the rest of the text illustrates.","It explains why the grandmother knitted.","It describes the ingredients of the bread.","It reveals the narrator's career."],"answer":"A","explanation":"Patience is illustrated by the bread. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.972d73f2a1","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data13-277","passage":"<p>A company that manufactures phone cases switched from plastic packaging to paper made from recycled cardboard. Surveys showed that customers noticed the change and viewed the brand more favorably. Shipping costs also fell slightly because the new packaging was lighter.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the final sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It describes an additional, practical benefit of the change.","It explains how cardboard is recycled.","It describes the phone cases.","It contradicts the survey results."],"answer":"A","explanation":"Lighter packaging lowered shipping costs. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.f9902280c6","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data13-278","passage":"<p>Linguists studying a remote village found that elderly residents used many words for types of snow and ice that younger residents did not know. As the climate warmed and people traveled less over frozen land, the precise terms were used less often. The researchers are recording elders' speech to preserve this detailed knowledge.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the second sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It lists the words for snow.","It explains why younger residents are less familiar with the terms.","It contradicts the first sentence.","It describes how researchers record speech."],"answer":"B","explanation":"Warming and less travel reduced use. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.c6e3464405","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data13-283","passage":"<p>Scientists studying desert tortoises found that the animals dig burrows that can stay cool even when surface temperatures are extremely high. Other species, including snakes, lizards, and insects, often use abandoned tortoise burrows to escape the heat. The researchers describe the tortoises as important to the survival of many other desert animals.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the second sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It explains how tortoises dig.","It describes tortoises' diets.","It shows how other species benefit from the burrows.","It contradicts the first sentence."],"answer":"C","explanation":"Snakes, lizards, and insects use them. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.a840660a57","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data13-286","passage":"<p>Farmers in one region began releasing ladybugs into greenhouses to control aphids instead of spraying insecticides. Aphid numbers fell, and the farmers saved money on chemicals. However, ladybugs sometimes flew away when food was scarce, so farmers learned to release them in smaller groups more frequently.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the final sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It explains why aphids damage plants.","It describes insecticide ingredients.","It restates the benefits.","It describes a challenge and how farmers adapted to it."],"answer":"D","explanation":"Ladybugs flew away, so releases changed. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.e94f27c619","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data13-287","passage":"<p>When a city offered free public Wi-Fi in parks, officials expected people to use it mainly for entertainment. Surveys found that many users were students completing homework and job seekers submitting applications, especially in neighborhoods where many households lacked home internet.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the first sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It explains how Wi-Fi works.","It presents an expectation that the survey findings complicated.","It describes the parks' size.","It summarizes the survey results."],"answer":"B","explanation":"Officials expected entertainment use. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.c9d192baee","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data13-289","passage":"<p class=\"src\">The following text is from a memoir.</p><p>My father could fix almost anything, but he rarely explained how. When I was twelve and the lawnmower broke, he handed me the manual and a screwdriver and went inside. I spent the entire afternoon covered in grease, furious. By evening the mower started. He came out, listened to it run, nodded once, and went back in. I have never been prouder of a nod.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the final sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It suggests the narrator was still angry.","It explains how lawnmowers work.","It describes the father's career.","It shows how much the father's small gesture of approval meant to the narrator."],"answer":"D","explanation":"\"Never been prouder of a nod.\" The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.30e9267864","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data13-291","passage":"<p>A study of museum visitors found that people who took photographs of artworks remembered fewer details about them later than people who simply looked. However, when visitors zoomed in on a specific part of an artwork while photographing it, their memory for that part improved. Researchers suggest that focused attention, not photography itself, affects memory.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the word \"However\" in the text?","choices":["It describes the museum's collection.","It introduces a finding that qualifies the general effect of photography on memory.","It contradicts the idea that visitors took photos.","It explains how cameras zoom."],"answer":"B","explanation":"Zooming in reversed the effect for that detail. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.2303e7b4aa","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data13-292","passage":"<p>Researchers studying why some neighborhoods have more street trees than others found that wealthier areas often had greater tree cover, partly because homeowners could afford to plant and maintain trees. In response, several cities launched programs to plant trees in neighborhoods with low tree cover and to fund their care during the first few years.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the second sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It describes actions taken to address the pattern described in the first sentence.","It contradicts the research findings.","It describes the costs of homes.","It explains how trees grow."],"answer":"A","explanation":"Programs respond to unequal tree cover. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.a5b304566c","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data13-293","passage":"<p>When a publishing company began releasing audiobooks narrated by the authors themselves, sales of those audiobooks rose compared with versions read by professional narrators. Listeners reported that hearing authors' own voices made the books feel more personal. Some reviewers noted, however, that not all authors were skilled readers.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the final sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It explains how audiobooks are recorded.","It supports the claim that sales rose.","It describes the books' plots.","It notes a limitation of author narration."],"answer":"D","explanation":"Not all authors read well. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.fa40f96cec","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data13-294","passage":"<p>Scientists examining ancient teeth found that people in one farming village had more cavities than hunter-gatherers who lived nearby at the same time. The farmers ate diets rich in grains, which break down into sugars that feed bacteria in the mouth. The finding suggests that changes in diet during the transition to farming affected dental health.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the second sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It explains why the farmers may have had more cavities.","It describes how teeth were excavated.","It compares tools used by the two groups.","It contradicts the first sentence."],"answer":"A","explanation":"Grains break down into sugars that feed bacteria. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.4fb8aabef6","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data13-297","passage":"<p>When a small bookstore installed a shelf labeled \"Staff Picks\" with handwritten notes explaining why employees loved each book, sales of those titles rose sharply. Customers said the notes felt like recommendations from a friend. Several books that had been sitting unsold for months became bestsellers at the store.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the final sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It describes the store's owner.","It contradicts the earlier sentences.","It explains how books are shipped.","It provides a striking example of the shelf's effect."],"answer":"D","explanation":"Unsold books became bestsellers. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.95b9179692","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data13-298","passage":"<p>Biologists studying salmon in a river with a newly removed dam found that fish began swimming upstream to spawning grounds they had not reached in decades. Within a few years, populations of insects, birds, and bears along the upper river also increased, as salmon carcasses and eggs provided food.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the second sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It explains how dams are built.","It describes fishing regulations.","It describes broader ecological effects of the salmon's return.","It contradicts the first sentence."],"answer":"C","explanation":"Insects, birds, and bears increased. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."},
{"id":"g.rw.text-structure.2.0c928a205d","section":"rw","domain":"craft","skill":"text-structure","difficulty":2,"group":"psg-passage_data13-301","passage":"<p>When a city planted wildflower meadows along highway medians instead of mowed grass, maintenance crews mowed only once a year instead of every few weeks. The city saved money on fuel and labor, and surveys of the medians found many more bees and butterflies than before. Some drivers initially complained that the medians looked overgrown, but complaints declined as the flowers bloomed.</p>","prompt":"Which choice best describes the function of the final sentence in the text as a whole?","choices":["It describes the highway's traffic.","It restates the cost savings.","It describes an initial objection and how it changed over time.","It explains how wildflowers are planted."],"answer":"C","explanation":"Complaints declined as flowers bloomed. The other choices either go beyond what the text says, contradict it, or focus on a detail rather than the point the question asks about."}
]);
